{"format":1,"manifest":{"name":"hello","publisher":"vyloxi","version":"1.0.0","displayName":"Hello Ferrum","description":"The example extension: a greeting command, a live word counter in the status bar and a panel with page statistics.","engines":{"ferrum":"^0.1.0"},"categories":["Tools"],"icon":"icon.png","repository":"https://github.com/voukengdongmofrankysteve/ferrum-market","license":"MIT","main":"extension.js","activationEvents":["onStartup"],"permissions":[],"contributes":{"commands":[{"command":"hello.say","title":"Say Hello","category":"Hello Ferrum"},{"command":"hello.upper","title":"Make Selection Upper Case","category":"Hello Ferrum"},{"command":"hello.stats","title":"Show Page Statistics","category":"Hello Ferrum"}],"keybindings":[{"command":"hello.say","key":"Ctrl+Alt+H"},{"command":"hello.upper","key":"Ctrl+Alt+U"}],"configuration":{"title":"Hello Ferrum","properties":{"hello.greeting":{"type":"string","default":"Hello","description":"The word used to greet."},"hello.loud":{"type":"boolean","default":false,"description":"Greet in capital letters."},"hello.counter":{"type":"boolean","default":true,"description":"Show the word counter in the status bar."}}}}},"files":{"icon.png":{"encoding":"base64","content":""},"extension.js":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"// Hello Ferrum: a small tour of the extension API.\n// Docs: https://ferrum.vyloxi.com/docs/api\n\nconst words = (text) => (text.match(/\\S+/g) || []).length;\n\nexports.activate = function (context) {\n  // 1. A command with an input box and a setting.\n  context.subscriptions.push(\n    ferrum.commands.register('hello.say', async () => {\n      const name = await ferrum.window.showInputBox({ prompt: 'Who should I greet?', value: 'world' });\n      if (name === undefined) return; // the person pressed Escape\n      let text = ferrum.settings.get('hello.greeting') + ', ' + name + '!';\n      if (ferrum.settings.get('hello.loud')) text = text.toUpperCase();\n      ferrum.window.showMessage(text);\n    }),\n  );\n\n  // 2. A command that edits the open file. One undoable step.\n  context.subscriptions.push(\n    ferrum.commands.register('hello.upper', async () => {\n      const doc = await ferrum.editor.active();\n      if (!doc || !doc.selectedText) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Select some text first.', 'warn');\n      await ferrum.editor.insert(doc.selectedText.toUpperCase());\n    }),\n  );\n\n  // 3. A status bar item that follows the open file.\n  const refresh = async () => {\n    if (!ferrum.settings.get('hello.counter')) return ferrum.window.setStatusBar('hello.words', { text: '' }) && undefined;\n    const doc = await ferrum.editor.active();\n    ferrum.window.setStatusBar('hello.words', {\n      text: doc ? words(doc.text) + ' words' : 'no file',\n      tooltip: 'Click for page statistics',\n      command: 'hello.stats',\n    });\n  };\n  context.subscriptions.push(ferrum.events.on('activeChanged', refresh), ferrum.events.on('save', refresh), ferrum.events.on('settingsChanged', refresh));\n  refresh();\n\n  // 4. A panel with HTML, talking to the extension with messages.\n  context.subscriptions.push(\n    ferrum.commands.register('hello.stats', async () => {\n      const panel = await ferrum.window.showPanel({\n        title: 'Page statistics',\n        html: `\n          <h2>Page statistics</h2>\n          <p id=\"out\">Loading...</p>\n          <button id=\"again\">Count again</button>\n          <script>\n            const out = document.getElementById('out');\n            document.getElementById('again').onclick = () => ferrumPanel.postMessage({ type: 'count' });\n            ferrumPanel.onMessage((m) => { if (m.type === 'result') out.textContent = m.text; });\n            ferrumPanel.postMessage({ type: 'count' });\n          </script>`,\n      });\n      panel.onMessage(async (m) => {\n        if (m.type !== 'count') return;\n        const doc = await ferrum.editor.active();\n        panel.postMessage({\n          type: 'result',\n          text: doc ? doc.name + ': ' + doc.lineCount + ' lines, ' + words(doc.text) + ' words, ' + doc.text.length + ' characters.' : 'Open a file first.',\n        });\n      });\n    }),\n  );\n};\n\nexports.deactivate = function () {};\n"},"README.md":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"# Hello Ferrum\n\nThe example extension for Ferrum. It is small on purpose: read `extension.js` next to this page to see how each feature is used. The source is in the [ferrum-market repository](https://github.com/voukengdongmofrankysteve/ferrum-market).\n\n- **Hello: Say Hello** asks for a name and greets it. The greeting word and loud mode are settings.\n- **Hello: Make Selection Upper Case** changes the selected text, as one undoable edit.\n- A **word counter** in the status bar follows the open file. Click it to open the statistics.\n- **Hello: Show Page Statistics** opens a panel with lines, words and characters of the open file.\n\n## Make your own\n\nRead the [documentation](https://ferrum.vyloxi.com/docs/getting-started), copy this folder, change `publisher` and `name` in `ferrum.json`, and publish it.\n\nNo permissions needed.\n"}}}